      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm working on a predictive model for property theft/larceny risk in a few urban ZIP codes for my firm. I'm looking at some recent census data alongside crime stats from the last 5 years. I'm seeing some significant shifts in the ethnic composition of these areas recently. From a purely statistical modeling standpoint, when looking at rising diversity or changes in ethnic makeup in a neighborhood, do you see that typically serve as a meaningful predictor for larceny rates in actuarial models?",
